@page
@using MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web.Pages
@using MerkaiTrial.Domain.Entities
@model MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web.Pages.Pipeline.IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Pipeline";

    var canDrag = Model.CanUpdate;
    var stages = Model.Stages.OrderBy(s => s.SortOrder).ToList();
    var emptyColumns = stages.Count(s => Model.GetDealsByStage(s.Key).Count == 0);
    var atLimit = AuthorizedPageModel.IsAtLimit(Model.DealQuotaUsed, Model.MaxDeals);
    var dealPct = AuthorizedPageModel.QuotaPercent(Model.DealQuotaUsed, Model.MaxDeals);
    var barClass = AuthorizedPageModel.QuotaBarClass(Model.DealQuotaUsed, Model.MaxDeals);
    var hasFilter = !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.SearchTerm)
                 || !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.StageFilter)
                 || !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.OwnerFilter);
}
@* =====================================================================
   PIPELINE BOARD (030)
   Location: MerkaiTrial.Admin.Web/Pages/Pipeline/Index.cshtml

   COMPLETE FILE — replaces the 020 version.

   WHAT WAS WRONG, IN ORDER OF HOW MUCH IT MATTERED

   1. ★ DRAG AND DROP DID NOT WORK AT ALL. The handlers were attached like
      this:

          <div class="deals-container"
               @@(canDrag ? "ondrop=\"drop(event)\" ondragover=\"allowDrop(event)\"" : "")>

      Razor HTML-ENCODES the result of @@(...). The browser therefore
      received

          ondrop=&quot;drop(event)&quot;

      so the attribute's value was the six-character string "drop(event)"
      INCLUDING the quotes — a JavaScript string literal that evaluates to
      itself and does nothing. Same for ondragover, ondragenter and the
      cards' ondragstart.

      Consequence: draggable="true" rendered correctly (that one is a
      normal attribute value, so encoding is harmless), so cards picked up
      and followed the cursor — but ondragstart never fired, so
      draggedElement stayed null, and drop() returned on its own first
      line even if it had been wired. Every drag silently did nothing and
      the card snapped back, which reads exactly like "the board is
      broken".

      Everything is attached with addEventListener now. No inline handler
      is built by string concatenation anywhere on this page.

   2. THE BOARD WRAPPED ONTO TWO ROWS AND STRETCHED. It was
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)) — so
      with six or more stages the columns wrapped, and a wrapped grid row
      stretches every column to the height of the tallest. Combined with
      min-height: 500px per column, a workspace with six stages and four
      deals spent about 1,200px of scrolling to say very little. A board
      scrolls sideways; it does not wrap. Empty columns now collapse
      behind a switch that counts them.

   3. IT LOADED BOOTSTRAP THREE TIMES. Bootstrap CSS and Bootstrap Icons
      from a CDN inside <body>, and then bootstrap.bundle.min.js as well —
      all three already loaded by _Layout.cshtml. Loading the bundle a
      second time replaces window.bootstrap, so any component instance the
      FIRST copy created is invisible to the second: a modal opened
      through getOrCreateInstance can end up with two backdrops, or
      refuse to close. That is the likeliest cause of any odd modal
      behaviour on this page.

   4. THE FILTERS EXISTED BUT HAD NO UI. OwnerFilter, StageFilter and
      SearchTerm are all [BindProperty(SupportsGet = true)] and the page
      passes them to GetAllAsync — but nothing on the page ever set them,
      so the only way to filter the board was to hand-write a URL.

   5. CARD DATES WERE RAW UTC, in the SERVER's culture:
      deal.ExpectedCloseDateUtc.ToString("MMM dd"). Everything else on the
      page goes through the tenant's timezone and culture, so a deal
      closing on the 1st showed as the 30th for a Thai or Indian
      workspace late in the day.

   6. SWITCHING TO THE TABLE VIEW DIDN'T STICK. A move reloads the board
      (so the totals catch up), which threw a table-view user back to the
      board every time. The choice is remembered now, and an early script
      sets it before the first paint so there is no flash.

   7. "Total Deals" SAT BESIDE A QUOTA BAR COUNTING SOMETHING ELSE.
      TotalDeals is the deals THIS user can see; DealQuotaUsed is the
      whole workspace. Both are still shown — they are both useful — but
      they are now labelled so nobody has to work out why 4 and 12 are
      both right.
   ===================================================================== *@

<style>
    .pb { max-width: 1600px; margin: 0 auto; }

    /* ── header ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pb-head { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .pb-title { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; margin: 0; line-height: 1.2; }
    .pb-sub { font-size: .84rem; color: #64748b; margin: .2rem 0 0; }

    /* ── stats ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pb-stats { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; border: 1px solid #e9ecef; border-radius: 12px;
                background: #fff; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .pb-stat { flex: 1 1 190px; padding: .7rem 1rem; border-right: 1px solid #f1f3f5; }
    .pb-stat:last-child { border-right: 0; }
    .pb-stat .lbl { font-size: .68rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em;
                    color: #94a3b8; font-weight: 650; }
    .pb-stat .val { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; line-height: 1.3; }
    .pb-stat .sub { font-size: .72rem; color: #94a3b8; }

    /* ── quota ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pb-quota { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .75rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
                border: 1px solid #e9ecef; border-radius: 12px; background: #fff;
                padding: .55rem .9rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: .8rem; }
    .pb-quota .bar { flex: 1 1 160px; min-width: 120px; }

    /* ── toolbar ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pb-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: .6rem .75rem;
              border: 1px solid #e9ecef; border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .pb-toggle .btn { --bs-btn-padding-y: .2rem; --bs-btn-padding-x: .6rem; font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .pb-count { font-size: .78rem; color: #64748b; }

    /* ── board ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    /* flex, not grid: a board scrolls sideways. A wrapped grid row
       stretches every column to the tallest, which is where the wall of
       white space came from. */
    .pb-board { display: flex; gap: .85rem; overflow-x: auto; padding-bottom: .75rem; align-items: flex-start; }
    .pb-col { flex: 0 0 292px; width: 292px; background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #eef1f4;
              border-radius: 12px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; max-height: 72vh; }
    .pb-col-head { padding: .65rem .8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #e9edf1;
                   border-top: 3px solid var(--tone, #94a3b8); border-radius: 12px 12px 0 0; flex: 0 0 auto; }
    .pb-col-title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; font-size: .84rem;
                    font-weight: 650; color: #334155; }
    .pb-col-pill { margin-left: auto; min-width: 22px; text-align: center; font-size: .72rem;
                   font-weight: 700; color: #fff; background: var(--tone, #94a3b8);
                   border-radius: 20px; padding: .05rem .45rem; }
    .pb-col-val { font-size: .72rem; color: #94a3b8; margin-top: .2rem; }
    .pb-gate { font-size: .68rem; color: #b45309; margin-top: .25rem; display: block; }
    .pb-drop { padding: .6rem; overflow-y: auto; flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 90px;
               border-radius: 0 0 12px 12px; transition: background-color .12s, box-shadow .12s; }
    .pb-drop.over { background: rgba(79,70,229,.07); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(79,70,229,.35); }
    .pb-drop.no-drop.over { background: rgba(220,53,69,.06); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(220,53,69,.35); }
    .pb-col-empty { padding: .9rem .6rem; text-align: center; color: #b9c2cc; font-size: .76rem; }

    /* ── card ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pb-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e9ecef; border-left: 4px solid var(--tone, #94a3b8);
               border-radius: 9px; padding: .65rem .7rem; margin-bottom: .55rem;
               transition: box-shadow .15s, transform .15s; }
    .pb-card:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .pb-card[draggable="true"] { cursor: grab; }
    .pb-card:hover { box-shadow: 0 3px 10px rgba(16,24,40,.09); transform: translateY(-1px); }
    .pb-card.dragging { opacity: .45; }
    .pb-card.refused { animation: pbRefuse 1.4s ease-out; }
    @@keyframes pbRefuse {
        0%   { box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(220,53,69,.55); }
        100% { box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08); }
    }
    .pb-card a.t { font-weight: 650; color: #0f172a; font-size: .88rem; text-decoration: none;
                   display: block; }
    .pb-card a.t:hover { color: #4f46e5; }
    .pb-card .co { font-size: .78rem; color: #64748b; margin-top: .15rem; overflow: hidden;
                   text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
    .pb-card .amt { font-size: .95rem; font-weight: 700; color: #4f46e5; margin-top: .3rem; }
    .pb-card.is-lost .amt { color: #94a3b8; }
    .pb-card .meta { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: .4rem;
                     font-size: .72rem; color: #94a3b8; margin-top: .45rem; }
    .pb-card .own { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .35rem; min-width: 0; }
    .pb-av { width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 50%; background: #4f46e5; color: #fff;
             display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: .62rem;
             font-weight: 700; flex: 0 0 auto; }
    .pb-card.is-lost .pb-av { background: #adb5bd; }
    .pb-q { font-size: .7rem; border-radius: 6px; padding: .2rem .4rem; margin-bottom: .4rem;
            display: block; }
    .pb-q.ok { background: #dcfce7; color: #15803d; }
    .pb-q.sent { background: #dbeafe; color: #1d4ed8; }

    /* ── table ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    .pb-shell { border: 1px solid #e9ecef; border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; overflow: hidden; }
    .pb-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 0; }
    .pb-table th { font-size: .7rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: #64748b;
                   font-weight: 650; padding: .6rem .8rem; background: #fbfcfd;
                   border-bottom: 1px solid #eceff2; white-space: nowrap; }
    .pb-table td { padding: .6rem .8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #f4f6f8; vertical-align: middle;
                   font-size: .85rem; }
    .pb-table tbody tr:hover { background: #fcfdfe; }
    .pb-table tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
    .pb-table .n { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 650; }
    .pb-table .d { white-space: nowrap; }
    .pb-clip { max-width: 190px; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
    .pb-table th.q-stick, .pb-table td.q-stick { position: sticky; right: 0; z-index: 2; background: #fff;
        box-shadow: -8px 0 8px -8px rgba(15,23,42,.18); }
    .pb-table th.q-stick { background: #fbfcfd; z-index: 3; }
    .pb-table tbody tr:hover td.q-stick { background: #fcfdfe; }

    .pb-empty { text-align: center; padding: 2.5rem 1rem; color: #94a3b8; }
    .pb-empty i.big { font-size: 2.4rem; color: #d7dde3; display: block; margin-bottom: .6rem; }

    .pb-hidden { display: none !important; }

    /* Set on <html> before either view is parsed, so somebody who prefers
       the table never sees the board paint first and swap. */
    html[data-pbview="table"] #pbBoard { display: none !important; }
    html[data-pbview="board"] #pbTable { display: none !important; }

    #pbRefused { position: sticky; top: .5rem; z-index: 1030; }

    @@media (max-width: 767.98px) {
        .pb-col { flex-basis: 86vw; width: 86vw; max-height: none; }
        .pb-stat { flex-basis: 50%; }
        .pb-title { font-size: 1.25rem; }
    }
</style>

<script>
    // Runs during parse, before either view exists. Only sets an attribute
    // the CSS above keys off, so it cannot throw on a half-built page.
    (function () {
        try {
            var p = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
            var u = p.get('View') || p.get('view') || p.get('VIEW');
            var v = u ? u.toLowerCase() : (localStorage.getItem('merkai.pipeline.view') || 'board');
            document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-pbview', v === 'table' ? 'table' : 'board');
        } catch (e) {
            document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-pbview', 'board');
        }
    })();
</script>

<div class="pb">

    @* ── header ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <div class="pb-head">
        <div>
            <h1 class="pb-title">Sales pipeline</h1>
            <p class="pb-sub">
                @if (hasFilter)
                {
                    <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning-emphasis border border-warning-subtle me-1">filtered</span>
                }
                @Model.TotalDeals @(Model.TotalDeals == 1 ? "deal" : "deals") you can see,
                worth @Model.FormatCurrency(Model.TotalValue, 0)
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ms-auto d-flex align-items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
            <span class="badge @Model.PlanBadgeClass px-3 py-2">@Model.PlanDisplayName</span>

            @if (Model.UserCanRead("settings"))
            {
                <a asp-page="/Settings/PipelineRules/Index" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
                   title="Sales process">
                    <i class="bi bi-diagram-3"></i>
                </a>
            }

            @if (!atLimit && Model.CanCreate)
            {
                <a asp-page="/Pipeline/Create" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary">
                    <i class="bi bi-plus-lg me-1"></i>New deal
                </a>
            }
            else if (atLimit)
            {
                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" disabled
                        title="Deal limit reached. @Model.UpgradePrompt">
                    <i class="bi bi-lock me-1"></i>Deal limit reached
                </button>
            }
        </div>
    </div>

    @* Where a refused drag explains itself. Hidden until needed. *@
    <div id="pbRefused" class="alert alert-warning alert-dismissible pb-hidden" role="alert">
        <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle-fill me-2"></i>
        <span id="pbRefusedText"></span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" id="pbRefusedClose" aria-label="Dismiss"></button>
    </div>

    @* ── stats ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    @* The first two tiles count what YOU can see; the quota strip below
       counts the whole workspace. Both are true and they disagree, so
       both say which they are. *@
    <div class="pb-stats">
        <div class="pb-stat">
            <div class="lbl">Deals you can see</div>
            <div class="val">@Model.TotalDeals</div>
            <div class="sub">@Model.FormatCurrency(Model.TotalValue, 0)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pb-stat">
            <div class="lbl">Weighted value</div>
            <div class="val" style="color:#0d6efd;">@Model.FormatCurrency(Model.WeightedValue, 0)</div>
            <div class="sub">open deals × probability</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pb-stat">
            <div class="lbl">Win rate</div>
            <div class="val text-success">@Model.WinRate%</div>
            <div class="sub">@Model.ClosedWonCount won of @(Model.ClosedWonCount + Model.ClosedLostCount) closed</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pb-stat">
            <div class="lbl">Average deal</div>
            <div class="val">@Model.FormatCurrency(Model.AvgDealSize, 0)</div>
            <div class="sub">across the deals above</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* ── quota ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <div class="pb-quota">
        <span class="text-muted fw-semibold text-uppercase" style="font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.06em;">
            Workspace deal quota
        </span>
        <div class="bar">
            <div class="progress" style="height:8px;">
                <div class="progress-bar @barClass" role="progressbar" style="width:@dealPct%"
                     aria-valuenow="@Model.DealQuotaUsed" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="@Model.MaxDeals"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <span class="@(dealPct >= 90 ? "text-danger fw-bold" : "text-muted")">
            @Model.DealQuotaUsed / @Model.MaxDeals used
        </span>
        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.UpgradePrompt))
        {
            <a href="/pricing" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary py-0">
                <i class="bi bi-arrow-up-circle me-1"></i>@Model.UpgradePrompt
            </a>
        }
    </div>

    @* ── toolbar ────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
    <div class="pb-bar">
        <div class="btn-group btn-group-sm pb-toggle" role="group" aria-label="View as board or table">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-view="board">
                <i class="bi bi-kanban me-1"></i>Board
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-view="table">
                <i class="bi bi-table me-1"></i>Table
            </button>
        </div>

        @* NEW. SearchTerm / StageFilter / OwnerFilter were bound from the
           query string and the page passed them to the API, but nothing ever
           set them — the only way to filter was to type a URL by hand. *@
        <form method="get" class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 flex-wrap" id="pbFilter">
            <input type="hidden" name="View" value="board" class="pb-view-field" />

            <div class="input-group input-group-sm" style="width:230px;">
                <span class="input-group-text"><i class="bi bi-search"></i></span>
                <input type="search" name="SearchTerm" value="@Model.SearchTerm" class="form-control"
                       placeholder="Deal or company" aria-label="Search deals" autocomplete="off" />
            </div>

            <select name="StageFilter" class="form-select form-select-sm" style="width:auto;"
                    aria-label="Filter by stage">
                <option value="">All stages</option>
                @foreach (var s in stages)
                {
                    <option value="@s.Key" selected="@(string.Equals(Model.StageFilter, s.Key, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))">
                        @s.Name
                    </option>
                }
            </select>

            <select name="OwnerFilter" class="form-select form-select-sm" style="width:auto;"
                    aria-label="Filter by owner">
                <option value="">All owners</option>
                @foreach (var u in Model.SalesTeam)
                {
                    <option value="@u.Id" selected="@(string.Equals(Model.OwnerFilter, u.Id.ToString(), StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))">
                        @u.FullName
                    </option>
                }
            </select>

            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" type="submit">Apply</button>

            @if (hasFilter)
            {
                <a asp-page="/Pipeline/Index" class="btn btn-sm btn-link px-1 pb-clear">Clear</a>
            }
        </form>

        <div class="ms-auto d-flex align-items-center gap-3">
            @if (Model.Rules is not null && Model.LiveMoves.Count > 0)
            {
                <span class="pb-count">
                    <i class="bi bi-diagram-3 me-1"></i>@Model.LiveMoves.Count
                    step@(Model.LiveMoves.Count == 1 ? "" : "s") in this process
                </span>
            }

            @if (emptyColumns > 0)
            {
                <div class="form-check form-switch mb-0 pb-hidden" id="pbEmptyWrap">
                    <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="pbShowEmpty" />
                    <label class="form-check-label pb-count" for="pbShowEmpty">
                        Show @emptyColumns empty column@(emptyColumns == 1 ? "" : "s")
                    </label>
                </div>
            }

            @if (!canDrag)
            {
                <span class="pb-count"><i class="bi bi-eye me-1"></i>read-only</span>
            }
        </div>
    </div>

    @if (!stages.Any())
    {
        <div class="pb-shell">
            <div class="pb-empty">
                <i class="bi bi-diagram-3 big"></i>
                <div class="fw-semibold text-body mb-1">This workspace has no pipeline stages</div>
                <div class="small">
                    <a asp-page="/Settings/Pipeline/Index">Add them under Settings</a> before creating deals.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        @* ── BOARD ──────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div id="pbBoard">
            <div class="pb-board">
                @foreach (var stage in stages)
                {
                    var isWon = stage.Category == StageCategory.Won;
                    var isLost = stage.Category == StageCategory.Lost;
                    var isClosed = isWon || isLost;
                    var dealsHere = Model.GetDealsByStage(stage.Key);
                    var hints = Model.EntryHintsFor(stage.Key);

                    // Open stages used to all share one grey accent, so every
                    // column looked the same. Walk a small palette by sort order
                    // instead — no per-stage colour column is needed.
                    var tone = isWon ? "#198754"
                             : isLost ? "#dc3545"
                             : new[] { "#64748b", "#0dcaf0", "#0d6efd", "#6f42c1", "#fd7e14", "#20c997" }
                                 [Math.Abs(stage.SortOrder) % 6];

                    <div class="pb-col @(dealsHere.Count == 0 ? "pb-hidden" : "")"
                         data-empty="@(dealsHere.Count == 0 ? "1" : "0")"
                         data-stage="@stage.Key"
                         data-stage-name="@stage.Name"
                         style="--tone:@tone;">
                        <div class="pb-col-head">
                            <div class="pb-col-title">
                                <i class="bi @(isWon ? "bi-trophy" : isLost ? "bi-x-circle" : "bi-circle")"></i>@stage.Name
                                <span class="pb-col-pill">@dealsHere.Count</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="pb-col-val">@Model.FormatCurrency(Model.GetStageValue(stage.Key), 0)</div>
                            @if (hints.Count > 0)
                            {
                                <span class="pb-gate" title="A deal needs @string.Join(", ", hints) before it can enter this stage.">
                                    <i class="bi bi-shield-check me-1"></i>needs @string.Join(", ", hints)
                                </span>
                            }
                        </div>

                        @* No inline ondrop/ondragover here. That is the bug this
                           round exists for: Razor encoded them into string
                           literals and nothing was ever wired up. The script at
                           the bottom attaches real listeners. *@
                        <div class="pb-drop" data-drop="@stage.Key">
                            @foreach (var deal in dealsHere)
                            {
                                var qs = Model.GetQuoteStatus(deal.Id);

                                <div class="pb-card @(isLost ? "is-lost" : "")"
                                     draggable="@(canDrag ? "true" : "false")"
                                     data-deal-id="@deal.Id"
                                     data-deal-title="@deal.Title"
                                     style="--tone:@tone;">

                                    @* Quote flags only matter on an open deal — a won
                                       deal's quote was obviously accepted. *@
                                    @if (!isClosed && qs?.HasAcceptedQuote == true)
                                    {
                                        <span class="pb-q ok"><i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-1"></i>Quote accepted</span>
                                    }
                                    else if (!isClosed && qs?.LatestQuoteStatus == "Sent")
                                    {
                                        <span class="pb-q sent"><i class="bi bi-send me-1"></i>Quote sent — awaiting reply</span>
                                    }

                                    @* A real link, not a div with a click handler: it
                                       opens in a new tab on middle-click, it has a
                                       status-bar target, and it is reachable by
                                       keyboard. The old card was a div whose click
                                       listener set window.location. *@
                                    <a class="t" asp-page="/Pipeline/Detail" asp-route-id="@deal.Id">@deal.Title</a>

                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(deal.CompanyName))
                                    {
                                        <div class="co" title="@deal.CompanyName">
                                            <i class="bi bi-building me-1"></i>@deal.CompanyName
                                        </div>
                                    }

                                    <div class="amt">@Model.FormatCurrency(deal.ExpectedValue, 0)</div>

                                    <div class="meta">
                                        <span class="own">
                                            <span class="pb-av">@deal.OwnerInitials</span>
                                            <span class="text-truncate">@deal.OwnerName</span>
                                        </span>
                                        <span class="flex-shrink-0">
                                            @* FormatDate, not ToString("MMM dd"): these are UTC
                                               instants and the old call printed them raw in the
                                               SERVER's culture. *@
                                            @if (isClosed && deal.ActualCloseDateUtc.HasValue)
                                            {
                                                <i class="bi @(isWon ? "bi-check-circle" : "bi-x-circle") me-1"></i>
                                                @Model.FormatDate(deal.ActualCloseDateUtc.Value)
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                <i class="bi bi-calendar me-1"></i>
                                                @Model.FormatDate(deal.ExpectedCloseDateUtc)
                                            }
                                        </span>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            }

                            @if (dealsHere.Count == 0)
                            {
                                <div class="pb-col-empty">Nothing here</div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </div>
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        @* ── TABLE ──────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div id="pbTable" class="pb-shell">
            <div class="table-responsive">
                <table class="pb-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Deal</th>
                            <th>Company</th>
                            <th>Stage</th>
                            <th class="n">Value</th>
                            <th class="n">Prob.</th>
                            <th>Owner</th>
                            <th>Closes</th>
                            <th class="q-stick text-end">Actions</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        @if (!Model.Deals.Any())
                        {
                            <tr>
                                <td colspan="8" class="pb-empty">
                                    @if (hasFilter)
                                    {
                                        <text>No deals match those filters.</text>
                                        <a asp-page="/Pipeline/Index">Clear them</a><text>.</text>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <text>No deals yet.</text>
                                    }
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        }
                        @foreach (var deal in Model.Deals)
                        {
                            <tr>
                                <td>
                                    <a asp-page="/Pipeline/Detail" asp-route-id="@deal.Id"
                                       class="text-decoration-none fw-semibold">@deal.Title</a>
                                </td>
                                <td><div class="pb-clip" title="@deal.CompanyName">@deal.CompanyName</div></td>
                                <td>
                                    <span class="badge @Model.StageBadgeClass(deal.Stage)">@Model.StageName(deal.Stage)</span>
                                </td>
                                <td class="n">@Model.FormatCurrency(deal.ExpectedValue, 0)</td>
                                <td class="n">@deal.Probability%</td>
                                <td><div class="pb-clip">@deal.OwnerName</div></td>
                                <td class="d">@Model.FormatDate(deal.ExpectedCloseDateUtc)</td>
                                <td class="q-stick text-end">
                                    <div class="d-flex gap-1 justify-content-end">
                                        <a asp-page="/Pipeline/Detail" asp-route-id="@deal.Id"
                                           class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" title="Open @deal.Title">
                                            <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right"></i>
                                        </a>
                                        @if (Model.CanUpdate && !Model.IsClosedStage(deal.Stage))
                                        {
                                            <a asp-page="/Pipeline/Edit" asp-route-id="@deal.Id"
                                               class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" title="Edit @deal.Title">
                                                <i class="bi bi-pencil"></i>
                                            </a>
                                        }
                                    </div>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        }
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</div>

@* ── the note dialog ───────────────────────────────────────────────
   One dialog for every move that asks for something. The prompt is the
   transition's own question, so a tenant asking "Which site did you
   survey?" gets that rather than a generic box. *@
<div class="modal fade" id="pbNoteModal" tabindex="-1" data-bs-backdrop="static" aria-labelledby="pbNoteTitle">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="pbNoteTitle">Move this deal</h5>
                <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Cancel"></button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
                <label class="form-label" for="pbNoteText" id="pbNotePrompt">Add a note for this change</label>
                <textarea id="pbNoteText" class="form-control" rows="3" maxlength="1000"
                          placeholder="A sentence is enough."></textarea>
                <div class="text-danger small mt-1 pb-hidden" id="pbNoteError">Please write a reason.</div>
                <div class="form-text">Kept on this deal's stage history.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-footer">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Cancel</button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="pbNoteConfirm">
                    <i class="bi bi-check-lg me-1"></i>Save &amp; move
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@* Carries the antiforgery token for the fetch below. *@
<form id="pbTokenForm" method="post" class="d-none">@Html.AntiForgeryToken()</form>

@* No Bootstrap CSS, icon font or JS bundle here. _Layout.cshtml loads all
   three. The old page loaded every one of them a second time, and a second
   copy of bootstrap.bundle replaces window.bootstrap — so an instance the
   first copy created becomes invisible to the second. *@
<script>
    (function () {
        'use strict';

        var root = document.documentElement;
        var CAN_DRAG = @(canDrag ? "true" : "false");

        // The tenant's live process, keyed "from|to". The SERVER checks all of
        // it again — this only decides whether to ask for a note before
        // posting, and whether to bother posting a move the process has no
        // step for.
        var MOVES = @Html.Raw(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.ProcessJson) ? "{}" : Model.ProcessJson);

        var VIEW_KEY = 'merkai.pipeline.view';
        var EMPTY_KEY = 'merkai.pipeline.showEmpty';

        function store(k, v) { try { localStorage.setItem(k, v); } catch (e) { } }
        function read(k) { try { return localStorage.getItem(k); } catch (e) { return null; } }

        // ── 1. board / table ─────────────────────────────────────────
        var board = document.getElementById('pbBoard');
        var table = document.getElementById('pbTable');
        var emptyWrap = document.getElementById('pbEmptyWrap');

        function applyView(v) {
            var isTable = v === 'table';
            root.setAttribute('data-pbview', isTable ? 'table' : 'board');
            if (board) board.classList.toggle('pb-hidden', isTable);
            if (table) table.classList.toggle('pb-hidden', !isTable);

            var btns = document.querySelectorAll('.pb-toggle [data-view]');
            for (var i = 0; i < btns.length; i++) {
                var on = btns[i].getAttribute('data-view') === v;
                btns[i].classList.toggle('btn-primary', on);
                btns[i].classList.toggle('btn-outline-secondary', !on);
                btns[i].setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
            }

            // The empty-column switch only means anything on the board.
            if (emptyWrap) emptyWrap.classList.toggle('pb-hidden', isTable);

            // Keep the filter form — and therefore Apply — on the view the
            // user is actually looking at. A move reloads the page, so without
            // this a table user was thrown back to the board every time.
            var vf = document.querySelectorAll('.pb-view-field');
            for (var f = 0; f < vf.length; f++) vf[f].value = v;

            var clears = document.querySelectorAll('a.pb-clear');
            for (var c = 0; c < clears.length; c++) {
                var href = (clears[c].getAttribute('href') || '').split('?')[0];
                clears[c].setAttribute('href', href + '?View=' + v);
            }

            store(VIEW_KEY, v);
        }

        document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
            var b = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('.pb-toggle [data-view]') : null;
            if (b) applyView(b.getAttribute('data-view'));
        });

        applyView(root.getAttribute('data-pbview') === 'table' ? 'table' : 'board');

        // ── 2. empty columns ─────────────────────────────────────────
        var showEmpty = document.getElementById('pbShowEmpty');
        function applyEmpty() {
            var show = showEmpty ? showEmpty.checked : false;
            var cols = document.querySelectorAll('.pb-col[data-empty="1"]');
            for (var i = 0; i < cols.length; i++) cols[i].classList.toggle('pb-hidden', !show);
            store(EMPTY_KEY, show ? '1' : '0');
        }
        if (showEmpty) {
            showEmpty.checked = read(EMPTY_KEY) === '1';
            showEmpty.addEventListener('change', applyEmpty);
            applyEmpty();
        }

        // ── 3. the refusal banner ────────────────────────────────────
        var refused = document.getElementById('pbRefused');
        var refusedText = document.getElementById('pbRefusedText');
        var refusedClose = document.getElementById('pbRefusedClose');

        function showRefused(msg) {
            if (!refused || !refusedText) return;
            refusedText.textContent = msg;
            refused.classList.remove('pb-hidden');
            refused.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
        }
        function hideRefused() { if (refused) refused.classList.add('pb-hidden'); }
        if (refusedClose) refusedClose.addEventListener('click', hideRefused);

        // ── 4. drag and drop, actually wired this time ───────────────
        var dragged = null;        // the card element
        var fromDrop = null;       // the .pb-drop it came out of

        if (CAN_DRAG) {
            document.addEventListener('dragstart', function (e) {
                var card = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('.pb-card[draggable="true"]') : null;
                if (!card) return;
                dragged = card;
                fromDrop = card.closest('.pb-drop');
                card.classList.add('dragging');
                // Firefox refuses to start a drag without data on the transfer.
                try {
                    e.dataTransfer.setData('text/plain', card.getAttribute('data-deal-id') || '');
                    e.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = 'move';
                } catch (err) { /* older browsers */ }
            });

            document.addEventListener('dragend', function () {
                if (dragged) dragged.classList.remove('dragging');
                var overs = document.querySelectorAll('.pb-drop.over');
                for (var i = 0; i < overs.length; i++) overs[i].classList.remove('over', 'no-drop');
            });

            // dragover MUST preventDefault or the drop event never fires. This
            // is the line the encoded inline attribute was failing to deliver.
            document.addEventListener('dragover', function (e) {
                var drop = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('.pb-drop') : null;
                if (!drop || !dragged) return;
                e.preventDefault();

                if (drop === fromDrop) { drop.classList.remove('no-drop'); drop.classList.add('over'); return; }

                // Show up front whether this column will take the card, using
                // the same matrix the drop handler checks.
                var from = fromDrop ? fromDrop.getAttribute('data-drop') : null;
                var to = drop.getAttribute('data-drop');
                var known = Object.keys(MOVES).length > 0;
                var allowed = !known || !from || !!MOVES[from + '|' + to];

                drop.classList.add('over');
                drop.classList.toggle('no-drop', !allowed);
            });

            document.addEventListener('dragleave', function (e) {
                var drop = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('.pb-drop') : null;
                if (drop && e.target === drop) drop.classList.remove('over', 'no-drop');
            });

            document.addEventListener('drop', function (e) {
                var drop = e.target && e.target.closest ? e.target.closest('.pb-drop') : null;
                if (!drop || !dragged) return;
                e.preventDefault();
                drop.classList.remove('over', 'no-drop');

                var card = dragged;
                var from = fromDrop;
                dragged = null;
                fromDrop = null;

                card.classList.remove('dragging');

                // Dropped back where it started. Posting would write a
                // Stage → same Stage row in the history.
                if (from === drop) return;

                var dealId = card.getAttribute('data-deal-id');
                if (!dealId) return;

                var fromStage = from ? from.getAttribute('data-drop') : null;
                var toStage = drop.getAttribute('data-drop');
                var fromCol = from ? from.closest('.pb-col') : null;
                var toCol = drop.closest('.pb-col');

                hideRefused();

                var move = fromStage ? MOVES[fromStage + '|' + toStage] : null;

                // Move the card now so the drag feels like it landed; put it
                // back if the answer is no.
                drop.appendChild(card);

                if (fromStage && Object.keys(MOVES).length > 0 && !move) {
                    var options = Object.keys(MOVES)
                        .filter(function (k) { return k.indexOf(fromStage + '|') === 0; })
                        .map(function (k) { return MOVES[k].label; });

                    revert(card, from);
                    showRefused(
                        'Moving from ' + (fromCol ? fromCol.getAttribute('data-stage-name') : 'there') +
                        ' to ' + (toCol ? toCol.getAttribute('data-stage-name') : 'there') +
                        " is not part of this workspace's sales process." +
                        (options.length ? ' From here you can: ' + options.join(', ') + '.' : ''));
                    return;
                }

                if (move && move.needsNote) {
                    askForNote(move, function (note) {
                        post(card, from, dealId, toStage, note);
                    }, function () {
                        revert(card, from);
                    });
                    return;
                }

                post(card, from, dealId, toStage, null);
            });
        }

        function revert(card, backTo) {
            if (!card || !backTo) return;
            backTo.appendChild(card);
            card.classList.add('refused');
            setTimeout(function () { card.classList.remove('refused'); }, 1500);
        }

        // ── 5. the note dialog ───────────────────────────────────────
        var noteEl = document.getElementById('pbNoteModal');
        var noteModal = null;
        var noteOnOk = null, noteOnCancel = null, noteSettled = false;

        function askForNote(move, onOk, onCancel) {
            if (!noteEl || typeof bootstrap === 'undefined') {
                // Don't strand the card in a column it was never saved into.
                if (onCancel) onCancel();
                showRefused('That move needs a note, and the dialog could not open. Move the deal from its own page instead.');
                return;
            }

            document.getElementById('pbNoteTitle').textContent = move.label || 'Move this deal';
            document.getElementById('pbNotePrompt').textContent =
                move.prompt || "Add a note for this change. It is kept on the deal's stage history.";
            document.getElementById('pbNoteText').value = '';
            document.getElementById('pbNoteError').classList.add('pb-hidden');

            noteOnOk = onOk; noteOnCancel = onCancel; noteSettled = false;

            noteModal = noteModal || bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance(noteEl);
            noteModal.show();
            setTimeout(function () { document.getElementById('pbNoteText').focus(); }, 250);
        }

        var noteConfirm = document.getElementById('pbNoteConfirm');
        if (noteConfirm) noteConfirm.addEventListener('click', function () {
            var text = (document.getElementById('pbNoteText').value || '').trim();
            if (!text) {
                document.getElementById('pbNoteError').classList.remove('pb-hidden');
                return;
            }
            noteSettled = true;
            if (noteModal) noteModal.hide();
            if (noteOnOk) noteOnOk(text);
        });

        // Cancel, Escape and the X all land here. Without it the card would sit
        // in its new column having never been saved, and the next refresh would
        // silently undo what the rep thought they had done.
        if (noteEl) noteEl.addEventListener('hidden.bs.modal', function () {
            if (noteSettled) return;
            if (noteOnCancel) noteOnCancel();
        });

        // ── 6. posting the move ──────────────────────────────────────
        function post(card, backTo, dealId, stage, note) {
            var token = document.querySelector('#pbTokenForm input[name="__RequestVerificationToken"]');
            if (!token || !token.value) {
                revert(card, backTo);
                showRefused('Could not verify the request. Please refresh the page and try again.');
                return;
            }

            var body = new FormData();
            body.append('dealId', dealId);
            body.append('stage', stage);
            if (note) body.append('note', note);

            fetch('?handler=UpdateStage', {
                method: 'POST',
                headers: { 'RequestVerificationToken': token.value },
                body: body
            }).then(function (res) {
                if (res.ok) {
                    // Reload so the column totals, win rate and weighted value
                    // all catch up with the move.
                    window.location.reload();
                    return null;
                }
                return res.json().catch(function () { return null; });
            }).then(function (data) {
                if (data === null) return;   // already reloading, or no JSON body
                revert(card, backTo);
                showRefused((data && data.error) ? data.error : 'That move was not allowed.');
            }).catch(function () {
                revert(card, backTo);
                showRefused('Something went wrong moving that deal. Please try again.');
            });
        }
    })();
</script>
